# Quality Gate

Before marking work done, committing, or opening a PR, run and pass:

```bash
npm run type-check
npm run lint:strict
npm run test
```

Fix all errors. Do not disable rules or skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks.

## Standards

- Match existing patterns in touched files; minimal scoped diffs
- No raw `console.*` in app code — use `@/lib/logger` (eslint `no-console: error`)
- Unused vars prefixed with `_` when intentionally unused
- Double quotes, 2-space indent, trailing commas in multiline
- Zod for API input validation; domain types in `src/domain/`
- No secrets in code or commits (`.env*`, `.cursor/secrets/`, `docs-local/`)

## When tests apply

- Bug fixes and behavior changes: add or update tests in `src/**/__tests__/`
- Pure UI/layout tweaks: tests optional unless logic changed
- Booking, checkout, auth, or payment flows: consider `npm run test:e2e:<suite>` when behavior is user-facing

## Failure loop

1. Run the failing command
2. Fix root cause (not suppressions)
3. Re-run until all three pass
4. Use `ReadLints` on edited files before finishing
